# Suggested crontab (decision 19 of the program). NOT INSTALLED by anything: the operator decides.
# Installation (the account that owns the checkout; the host is assumed to be on UTC): crontab -e, then paste
# the TWO uncommented lines below with YOUR paths. Check: crontab -l | grep -c 'monday.sh\|smoke.sh' = 2.
# The scripts read their layout from ops/env.sh (ops/env.local or exported variables): set YTM_ENV or export
# the variables in the crontab when the checkout is not the shipped layout (see ops/env.example).
#
# 1. Monday 06:00 UTC (before the day's chains and promotions): ops/monday.sh (cycle 53, B9-15) = wait for a free
#    host (no ytm-harness-*, no chain, no build), prod harness full tier (core + offline, about 20 min), weekly.sh
#    (ONE line appended to $YTM_PROGRAM_DIR/WEEKLY.md; a block in ALERT.md when: no full report or one older than
#    8 days, steps gated for more than a week, harness < 100 %, served version != last "PROD = <sha>" of CYCLES.md,
#    disk < 10 % free, 0 download with failures, stats monitor DOWN with a Kuma key), then smoke.sh HTTP with
#    SMOKE_ALERT=1. Detailed log: $YTM_PROGRAM_DIR/logs/monday-<date>.log (10 kept); cron only gets the summary.
#    Never redirect stdout to WEEKLY.md (the line would be duplicated). No mail; no Kuma key on the host (the Kuma
#    column then reads "n/a (token)"). WEEKLY_DB_RO=1 is set by monday.sh (retention column: read-only database).
0 6 * * 1 /bin/sh /path/to/checkout/ops/monday.sh >> /path/to/checkout/ops/monday-cron.log 2>&1  # music app monday (cycle 53)
#
# 2. Every day 06:30 UTC: prod smoke HTTP + browser (cycle 43, B7-15/B7-16); the browser is SKIPPED (not a failure)
#    when a ytm-harness-* already runs (on Mondays monday.sh normally finishes before 06:30); ALERT.md block on
#    failure. The URL is the production base URL ($YTM_PROD_URL of ops/env.sh).
30 6 * * * SMOKE_BROWSER=1 SMOKE_ALERT=1 /bin/sh /path/to/checkout/ops/smoke.sh http://127.0.0.1:8080 >> /path/to/checkout/ops/smoke-cron.log 2>&1  # music app smoke (cycle 43)
#
# Reading: tail -3 $YTM_PROGRAM_DIR/WEEKLY.md ; ls -l $YTM_PROGRAM_DIR/ALERT.md ;
#   tail -5 ops/monday-cron.log ; ls -t $YTM_PROGRAM_DIR/logs/monday-*.log | head -1
